CORE
main.c
--rounds 2 --unwind 3
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^Round bound (static): count=3 path=3 (at max rounds) max=3 
--
path capped
^warning: ignoring
--
The pingpong program of round-bound needs 4 rounds (path=4, count=4). With
the cap at 3 both are clamped to 3 and the line says so; the search stops as
soon as it has found a path with two backward edges, so it never falls back
to count ("path capped" must not appear).
